{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"The last open question is now narrowed by reading rather than by another probe, and the answer explains both uninstrumented zeros. The gap asked whether asymmetric write latencies bring the regression out under natural timing. Both writers use the same stable store and the same current-term key, so the term the node holds is whichever write that store applied last, and in a store that serialises writes that is decided by the order in which the two writes take effect rather than by their arrival times or durations. Overlap is therefore necessary but not sufficient: the term falls only when the main loop's lower write is applied after the off-thread higher one, which requires the main loop's write to be deferred behind the fast path's - contending on a lock or a write pipeline the heartbeat's write reaches first. That is why the uniform slow store stayed clean, since with equal treatment the later-arriving heartbeat write is also the later-applied one and the higher term survives, and why continuous delivery stayed clean for the other reason, that it keeps the campaign from starting at all. The discriminating shape is therefore a store whose write path defers the main thread's application behind the fast path's, not a denser schedule and not a uniformly slower store, and I recorded that as the answer to the gap along with a behaviour entry stating the mechanism, keeping the defect claim on the three receipts that establish the fall rather than on this reading. The answer is explicitly conditional: no execution has produced the fall under natural timing yet, the ordering argument assumes both writers share the store, and the practical rate under a contended store remains unmeasured, all of which I wrote down rather than leaving implicit. Everything else in the run is unchanged: the six witnessed behaviours with their receipts and controls, the protocol-gate bypass and the verification count drawing on sources outside the voter set, the scoped log-cache negative, and the two knowledge corrections.\"}"}}
